notes-api installed. One-time setup (as root):

1. Let the unprivileged service bind port 443:
     kldload mac_portacl
     echo 'mac_portacl_load="YES"' >> /boot/loader.conf
     sysctl net.inet.ip.portrange.reservedhigh=0
     sysctl security.mac.portacl.port_high=1023
     sysctl security.mac.portacl.rules="uid:$(id -u notes):tcp:443"
   and put the same three sysctl settings in /etc/sysctl.conf.

2. Create the CA and the TLS certificate (IP the clients will use):
     notes-cert init 192.168.88.60
   Then install the printed public ca.crt on your client devices.

3. Set the login (Basic auth over TLS; the file is not part of the package).
   Pick a password of 12+ characters; this one is generated:
     ( umask 077; printf 'notes:%s\n' "$(openssl rand -base64 18)" \
         > /usr/local/etc/notes-api.auth )
     chown notes /usr/local/etc/notes-api.auth
   Read it yourself with: cat /usr/local/etc/notes-api.auth

4. Enable and start:
     sysrc notes_api_enable=YES
     sysrc notes_api_baseurl="https://192.168.88.60:8443"
     service notes_api start

Data: /var/db/notes-api/notes.json (kept on pkg delete).
Log:  /var/log/notes-api.log
